c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440461 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440399 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440461 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440407 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440461 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440461 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440461 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440461 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440461 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440461 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186440450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440461 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "db389e57-4899-5138-b87d-2318a36bc5bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440462 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440462 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82699" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440462 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440462 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\}$ is given above. Find $[x]_{C}$ given that $x=4{b}_{2}-2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440462 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "38a4fba0-c09e-5c16-89d3-da5b6bc68d95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440462 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that since $x=4{b}_{2}-2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{3},$ we have\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nGiven the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C,$ we find the coordinates of $x$ relative to $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}[\\,x\\,]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440463 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440457 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440463 #edb/ref 1069 "q-113707" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440463 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440463 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,C=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe bases $B$ and $C$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B$ are given above. Find $[x]_{C}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440463 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4f73a710-afa9-5a82-9ac8-46435d104af8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186440463 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose columns are the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ relative to the basis $C.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}[\\,x\\,]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
